{"id": "EUVD-2026-103917", "enisaUuid": "980bd362-b4ef-3cce-ac17-470225c5a811", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: imu: adis16480: fix unprotected debugfs reads\n\nThe firmware_revision and firmware_date file operations are open coded\nand never call debugfs_file_get(), which debugfs_create_file_unsafe()\nrequires. debugfs_remove_recursive() therefore does not wait for a read\nin progress, and unbind frees the iio_dev underneath it.\n\nUse debugfs_create_file() instead.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:44:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:28", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a782244972715c76bdaf8b662e9b22e260c5296", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7e507c6da8875da93b4130c8185e82a9dfd565c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce308ce18dedc18e9eeff8473892975e6fdd7aef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/396b83106f5e7d16467049f0caabd10533c01a0e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e1dea54496f90a62318cf4eeaa1e9ef8316e92b6"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cjjc-mjvc-265x", "CVE-2026-98663"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0cf50e66-d394-341e-96d9-05f8a150f25e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1fccd1a7-4db5-3350-9df4-cd9be152159b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.16"}, {"id": "3369f2aa-b783-3f95-bab3-f66e60c76066", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "5bb0e9c4-54d1-3bc7-b3d2-ed8c155e1ce1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "61dcb6f1-17c7-3d04-83e8-f3a00cc82fa6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9bf94f836e32ea168ec7448a523c11480317ad79 <ce308ce18dedc18e9eeff8473892975e6fdd7aef"}, {"id": "8149a557-34a2-36c1-8f17-a20d7b4b260a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name